{"lines": ["So what did the Bloop turn out to be? Ice.", "NOAA's own page says the sounds recorded in the summer of 1997 are consistent with icequakes made by large icebergs as they crack and fracture.", "That comes from comparison. Hydrophones in the Scotia Sea picked up numerous icequakes, with spectrograms very similar to the Bloop. They used those icequakes to track an iceberg named A53a as it broke apart near South Georgia Island in early 2008. Some of them were detected on several sensors more than five thousand kilometres away.", "Other hydrophones in the Bransfield Strait and the Scotia Sea, between 2005 and 2009, found icequakes a prominent part of the ocean soundscape. Icebergs grounding and breaking up release as much acoustic energy as large geophysical events.", "So the Bloop was not a new sound. It was a very old one, made big by the distance.", "Rule four. Before you invent something new, compare it with the sounds you already know."], "words": [["So", 0.0, 0.16], ["what", 0.16, 0.36], ["did", 0.36, 0.5], ["the", 0.5, 0.6], ["Bloop", 0.6, 0.82], ["turn", 0.82, 1.08], ["out", 1.08, 1.24], ["to", 1.24, 1.4], ["be?", 1.4, 1.6], ["Ice.", 1.96, 2.16], ["NOAA's", 2.16, 2.74], ["own", 2.74, 3.32], ["page", 3.32, 3.9], ["says", 3.9, 4.36], ["the", 4.36, 4.56], ["sounds", 4.56, 4.88], ["recorded", 4.88, 5.28], ["in", 5.28, 5.66], ["the", 5.66, 5.76], ["summer", 5.76, 6.02], ["of", 6.02, 6.22], ["1997", 6.22, 7.08], ["are", 7.86, 8.12], ["consistent", 8.12, 8.4], ["with", 8.4, 8.92], ["icequakes", 8.92, 9.52], ["made", 9.52, 9.78], ["by", 9.78, 10.06], ["large", 10.06, 10.26], ["icebergs", 10.26, 11.2], ["as", 11.2, 11.48], ["they", 11.48, 11.66], ["crack", 11.66, 11.88], ["and", 11.88, 12.28], ["fracture.", 12.28, 12.52], ["That", 13.62, 13.72], ["comes", 13.72, 13.94], ["from", 13.94, 14.2], ["comparison.", 14.2, 14.52], ["Hydrophones", 15.32, 15.84], ["in", 15.84, 16.0], ["the", 16.0, 16.08], ["Scotia", 16.08, 16.28], ["Sea", 16.28, 16.7], ["picked", 16.7, 1